{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T11:48:56.097Z","ordinal":8405,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_017eccd7b592b193016a7b0c14b5f88191b5d4a9ec31205daa","status":"completed","call_id":"call_bNYacGeG1q0yLHEMlIlhqZLO","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/dev/Orva/docs/CONFIG.md\\n@@\\n-| `idle_ttl_seconds` | 120 | Worker idle this long gets reaped |\\n-| `target_concurrency` | 10 | Requests per worker before scale-up triggers |\\n+| `idle_ttl_seconds` | 600 | No-demand interval before an opted-in pool scales to zero |\\n | `scale_to_zero` | `false` | `true` = pool can drain to 0 (cold-start on next request) |\\n+\\n+Pool Controller v2 chooses capacity automatically from 60-second arrival\\n+rate × service p95, 6-second arrival rate × (service p95 + spawn p95), and\\n+immediate busy + queued pressure, with a 70% internal utilization target.\\n+`target_concurrency` was removed; stale requests receive `400 VALIDATION`\\n+with migration guidance.\\n+\\n+`scale_to_zero=true` owns `min_warm=0`. Turning it off restores a minimum of\\n+at least one. Sending both fields with an incompatible pair is rejected.\\n@@\\n-  -d '{\\\"function_id\\\":\\\"019df200-7b00-7e00-9c00-aab1cd2e3f40\\\",\\\"min_warm\\\":2,\\\"max_warm\\\":32,\\\"idle_ttl_seconds\\\":60}'\\n+  -d '{\\\"function_id\\\":\\\"019df200-7b00-7e00-9c00-aab1cd2e3f40\\\",\\\"min_warm\\\":2,\\\"max_warm\\\":32,\\\"idle_ttl_seconds\\\":600}'\\n*** Update File: /home/dev/Orva/docs/API.md\\n@@\\n   \\\"function_id\\\": \\\"019df200-7b00-7e00-9c00-aab1cd2e3f40\\\",\\n   \\\"min_warm\\\": 2,\\n   \\\"max_warm\\\": 32,\\n-  \\\"idle_ttl_seconds\\\": 120,\\n-  \\\"target_concurrency\\\": 10,\\n+  \\\"idle_ttl_seconds\\\": 600,\\n   \\\"scale_to_zero\\\": false\\n }\\n ```\\n \\n Fields are partial — unspecified ones keep the prior value (or default\\n-for new rows).\\n+for new rows). Defaults are min 1, max 50, idle TTL 600 seconds, and\\n+scale-to-zero off. Pool Controller v2 derives desired capacity from demand;\\n+the removed `target_concurrency` field returns `400 VALIDATION`.\\n*** Update File: /home/dev/Orva/docs/RUNTIMES.md\\n@@\\n-Per-function pool sizing is autoscaled based on EWMA request rate +\\n-in-flight concurrency. You can tune the floor/ceiling via\\n+Per-function pool sizing uses 60-second stable demand, 6-second burst demand,\\n+queue pressure, service p95, and cold-start p95. You tune only the policy\\n+floor/ceiling via\\n@@\\n-  \\\"idle_ttl_seconds\\\": 120,\\n-  \\\"target_concurrency\\\": 10\\n+  \\\"idle_ttl_seconds\\\": 600,\\n+  \\\"scale_to_zero\\\": false\\n }\\n*** Update File: /home/dev/Orva/docs/CLI.md\\n@@\\n-orva pool set --fn greeter --idle-ttl 300 --target-concurrency 4\\n+orva pool set --fn greeter --idle-ttl 300\\n*** Update File: /home/dev/Orva/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\\n@@\\n-| `pool_config`        | per-fn autoscaler tuning (min_warm, max_warm, target_concurrency) |\\n+| `pool_config`        | per-fn pool policy (min_warm, max_warm, idle TTL, scale-to-zero) |\\n*** Update File: /home/dev/Orva/docs/OPERATIONS.md\\n@@\\n-| `pools[].idle` for each pool | <= `pools[].dynamic_max`. If exceeded, the pool stability fix didn't deploy |\\n+| `pools[].idle + busy + spawning` | <= `pools[].effective_max`; queued should drain after a burst |\\n@@\\n-| `503 POOL_AT_CAPACITY` | this function's pool at `dynamic_max` and ctx fired waiting | raise `pool_config.max_warm` for that fn, or accept the backpressure |\\n+| `503 POOL_AT_CAPACITY` | this function reached its effective host/operator ceiling and the queue deadline expired | inspect `limiting_reason`; raise `max_warm` only when it says `operator_max`, otherwise add host capacity or reduce worker limits |\\n@@\\n-If PIDs are >300 and idle is >dynamic_max, the pool over-spawned past\\n+If PIDs are >300 and total workers exceed `effective_max`, the pool over-spawned past\\n@@\\n-**Recovery.** The autoscaler will catch up within ~30 s of load\\n+**Recovery.** The controller waits 30 seconds below target, then removes no\\n+more than 20% of workers per evaluation. It should converge without dropping\\n+busy work. If it doesn't:\\n-ending. If it doesn't:\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019ff047-606e-7151-aa76-510d68951809"}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T11:48:58.321Z","ordinal":8406,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019fef25-06a9-7cf3-99a2-3ea61f12f122","turn_id":"019ff047-606e-7151-aa76-510d68951809","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-0ea859e3-3d1f-4398-8f3f-5ec21aac3f17","changes":{"/home/dev/Orva/docs/RUNTIMES.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -170,4 +170,5 @@\n \n-Per-function pool sizing is autoscaled based on EWMA request rate +\n-in-flight concurrency. You can tune the floor/ceiling via\n+Per-function pool sizing uses 60-second stable demand, 6-second burst demand,\n+queue pressure, service p95, and cold-start p95. You tune only the policy\n+floor/ceiling via\n `PUT /api/v1/pool/config`:\n@@ -179,4 +180,4 @@\n   \"max_warm\": 32,\n-  \"idle_ttl_seconds\": 120,\n-  \"target_concurrency\": 10\n+  \"idle_ttl_seconds\": 600,\n+  \"scale_to_zero\": false\n }\n","move_path":null},"/home/dev/Orva/docs/CLI.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -580,3 +580,3 @@\n orva pool set --fn greeter --min-warm 2 --max-warm 20 --scale-to-zero\n-orva pool set --fn greeter --idle-ttl 300 --target-concurrency 4\n+orva pool set --fn greeter --idle-ttl 300\n ```\n","move_path":null},"/home/dev/Orva/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -206,3 +206,3 @@\n | `routes`             | custom URL → function-id mappings (`/webhooks/stripe`) |\n-| `pool_config`        | per-fn autoscaler tuning (min_warm, max_warm, target_concurrency) |\n+| `pool_config`        | per-fn pool policy (min_warm, max_warm, idle TTL, scale-to-zero) |\n | `system_config`      | global tuning knobs (versions_to_keep, gc_interval_seconds, etc.) |\n","move_path":null},"/home/dev/Orva/docs/OPERATIONS.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -25,3 +25,3 @@\n | `latency_ms.p99` | <= 5 × `latency_ms.p50`. If p99 is 10× p50 the pool is saturated |\n-| `pools[].idle` for each pool | <= `pools[].dynamic_max`. If exceeded, the pool stability fix didn't deploy |\n+| `pools[].idle + busy + spawning` | <= `pools[].effective_max`; queued should drain after a burst |\n \n@@ -34,3 +34,3 @@\n | `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` | host-wide concurrency cap hit | client should back off + retry. The ceiling is derived from CPU count (`NumCPU × 64`, floor 200) and is not operator-tunable today — add CPUs to raise it |\n-| `503 POOL_AT_CAPACITY` | this function's pool at `dynamic_max` and ctx fired waiting | raise `pool_config.max_warm` for that fn, or accept the backpressure |\n+| `503 POOL_AT_CAPACITY` | this function reached its effective host/operator ceiling and the queue deadline expired | inspect `limiting_reason`; raise `max_warm` only when it says `operator_max`, otherwise add host capacity or reduce worker limits |\n | `503 MEMORY_EXHAUSTED` | host RAM at 80% reservation | scale-down idle pools, increase host RAM, or reduce per-fn `memory_mb` |\n@@ -52,3 +52,3 @@\n \n-If PIDs are >300 and idle is >dynamic_max, the pool over-spawned past\n+If PIDs are >300 and total workers exceed `effective_max`, the pool over-spawned past\n its cap. This was a real bug fixed in early Round-G builds — if you're\n@@ -56,4 +56,5 @@\n \n-**Recovery.** The autoscaler will catch up within ~30 s of load\n-ending. If it doesn't:\n+**Recovery.** The controller waits 30 seconds below target, then removes no\n+more than 20% of workers per evaluation. It should converge without dropping\n+busy work. If it doesn't:\n \n","move_path":null},"/home/dev/Orva/docs/API.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -325,4 +325,3 @@\n   \"max_warm\": 32,\n-  \"idle_ttl_seconds\": 120,\n-  \"target_concurrency\": 10,\n+  \"idle_ttl_seconds\": 600,\n   \"scale_to_zero\": false\n@@ -332,3 +331,5 @@\n Fields are partial — unspecified ones keep the prior value (or default\n-for new rows).\n+for new rows). Defaults are min 1, max 50, idle TTL 600 seconds, and\n+scale-to-zero off. Pool Controller v2 derives desired capacity from demand;\n+the removed `target_concurrency` field returns `400 VALIDATION`.\n \n","move_path":null},"/home/dev/Orva/docs/CONFIG.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -93,6 +93,14 @@\n | `max_warm` | 50 | Hard ceiling on warm pool size |\n-| `idle_ttl_seconds` | 120 | Worker idle this long gets reaped |\n-| `target_concurrency` | 10 | Requests per worker before scale-up triggers |\n+| `idle_ttl_seconds` | 600 | No-demand interval before an opted-in pool scales to zero |\n | `scale_to_zero` | `false` | `true` = pool can drain to 0 (cold-start on next request) |\n \n+Pool Controller v2 chooses capacity automatically from 60-second arrival\n+rate × service p95, 6-second arrival rate × (service p95 + spawn p95), and\n+immediate busy + queued pressure, with a 70% internal utilization target.\n+`target_concurrency` was removed; stale requests receive `400 VALIDATION`\n+with migration guidance.\n+\n+`scale_to_zero=true` owns `min_warm=0`. Turning it off restores a minimum of\n+at least one. Sending both fields with an incompatible pair is rejected.\n+\n ```bash\n@@ -100,3 +108,3 @@\n   http://localhost:8443/api/v1/pool/config \\\n-  -d '{\"function_id\":\"019df200-7b00-7e00-9c00-aab1cd2e3f40\",\"min_warm\":2,\"max_warm\":32,\"idle_ttl_seconds\":60}'\n+  -d '{\"function_id\":\"019df200-7b00-7e00-9c00-aab1cd2e3f40\",\"min_warm\":2,\"max_warm\":32,\"idle_ttl_seconds\":600}'\n ```\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/dev/Orva/docs/CONFIG.md\nM /home/dev/Orva/docs/API.md\nM /home/dev/Orva/docs/RUNTIMES.md\nM /home/dev/Orva/docs/CLI.md\nM /home/dev/Orva/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\nM /home/dev/Orva/docs/OPERATIONS.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1786448936757,"completed_at_ms":1786448938321}}
