{"timestamp":"2026-08-11T12:27:41.267Z","ordinal":9500,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019fef25-06a9-7cf3-99a2-3ea61f12f122","turn_id":"019ff047-606e-7151-aa76-510d68951809","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_017eccd7b592b193016a7b153ae7008191934261e73ecacbea","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The first sandbox E2E attempt exposed a test-environment mistake—the temporary data directory pointed at a nonexistent rootfs, so the expected crash/timeout responses became pool errors. With the real provisioned rootfs mounted, the suite is now 9/9 green, and live metrics confirm the controller reports queue, service, cold-start, limiting reason, and effective host capacity correctly."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1786451259016,"completed_at_ms":1786451261267}}
